    "note": "v1.1 では WAV ヘッダ全85曲実測が spec 要求（24-bit）と一致（85/85 match）したため、本 record の時点では停止事由なし。v1 での停止の経緯は h3b_freeze_record.superseded.1.json の stop_event、および e2_measurement_report.md の v1 タイムラインに保持している。",
    "occurred": false
  },
  "supersede_reason": "v1 (metric_version h3b-extractor-spec/1) required WAV 16-bit/mono/48000Hz (spec §2-1). E2 header measurement (metadata-only RIFF/fmt read, no decode) of all 85 training+validation pjsNNN_song.wav found the real PJS corpus is uniformly 24-bit/mono/48000Hz — 0/85 matched the v1 requirement. v1's extractor correctly fail-closed-stopped before any decode (see h3b_freeze_record.superseded.1.json stop_event and e2_measurement_report.md for the full v1 timeline). Fable design judgement (2026-08-27): the stop was correct behaviour; the 24-bit measurement is a correction to spec's physical-layer assumption, not a change to channel semantics / extraction formulas / normalization method, and therefore is NOT a design-revision matter under 裁定 §5. Spec corrected to v1.1 (§2-1 now requires 24-bit and pins an exact manual byte-decode formula); no audio was ever decoded under v1, so 'freeze precedes extraction' is preserved by re-freezing under v1.1 before any PJS decode begins.",
  "supersedes": "h3b_freeze_record.superseded.1.json",
